WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.916
[PIANO PLAYING]

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.230
LEONARD AUSTIN: Ravelin is
a fraud-detection company.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:11.110
We specialize in detecting
credit card fraud.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.940
When a customer tries
to buy something

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.010
from one of our
merchants, the merchant

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.070
will then stream us
all of that data,

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.820
and we will use a load
of machine learning

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.670
behind the scenes to try and
analyze transactions and make

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.730
predictions around whether
that user is a genuine user

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.230
or fraudulent user.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.330
Security is really
important for us

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.630
because our clients are trusting
us with all of their data.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.210
So we go to
extraordinary lengths

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.070
to ensure that the
data that we hold

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.010
is encrypted and secured
in closed-source projects.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.640
So on-prem has the
problem of having

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.530
to manage your own security.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.260
The actual cloud itself and
the way that Google structures

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.630
the file system
means that one file

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.090
isn't stored on one computer.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.680
It's stored across
multiple disks, which

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.960
means even if someone
was able to get access

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.180
to a particular disk,
physical access,

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.810
they wouldn't actually be able
to get any data from that.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.610
There's a number of
services that GCP offered

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.360
we couldn't get elsewhere,
like the Identity-Aware Proxy

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.220
and encryption at
rest by default,

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.610
but also the further step that
enables us to supply encryption

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.950
keys to Google, so that
Google can't even unencrypt

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.210
the data if they wanted to.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.970
So those were all
really strong factors

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:21.610
that suggest that Google
really cares about security.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:25.710
And it enables us to trust
Google with all of our data.

